WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.150
(dynamic orchestral music)

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.160
- [Narrator] There is a
wise old Japanese saying:

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.113
the nail that sticks
out gets hammered down.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.430
Well, down in Tokyo, there's
one nail that sticks out

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.080
just about as far as you can imagine,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.490
an inventor known across the country,

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.937
a mad genius with a
staggering number of patents.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:23.854
(foreign language)

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.302
That includes a wig for self defense.

00:00:33.302 --> 00:00:35.410
(light orchestral music)

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.750
Meet Yoshiro Nakamatsu.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.690
You may notice his name
is spelled NakaMats.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.610
He dropped the letter U because he says

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.060
an eight-letter name
is easier to remember,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.809
but he still wants you to pronounce it:

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:49.730
(foreign language)

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.520
You got it, Doc.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.640
Dr. NakaMats's quirky inventions

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.603
brought him worldwide recognition;

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.500
inventions like the Pyon Pyon boots,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.050
with springs that put an
extra bounce in your step.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.820
There's Dr. NakaMats's Cerebrex.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.550
It looks like a La-Z-Boy, but the doc says

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.093
the darn thing enhances brain power.

00:01:13.344 --> 00:01:15.490
Then there's the gold golf putter

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.073
that pings when you strike the ball.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:21.210
Huh, would you look at that!

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.260
You know you've made it

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.100
when the streets are named after you.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.980
But make no mistake.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.220
Dr. NakaMats's inventions aren't all

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.040
noisy golf clubs and bouncy shoes.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.760
He claims to have
invented the floppy disk.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.423
That's right, that floppy disk.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:38.923
Retractable landing gear.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.690
A widely used kerosene pump.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.000
And even the digital watch.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.833
(beeping)

00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:47.730
To maintain his hyper-creativity,

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.043
Dr. NakaMats keeps his
mind and body in shape.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.140
That lightweight inventor
Thomas Edison said

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.930
genius is 1 percent inspiration
and 99 percent perspiration.

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:02.957
Is that your secret, Dr. NakaMats?

00:02:02.966 --> 00:02:05.883
(foreign language)

00:03:00.061 --> 00:03:03.955
("Symphpny No. 5", by Beethoven)

00:03:03.955 --> 00:03:06.872
(foreign language)

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.924
(light piano music)

00:03:48.924 --> 00:03:51.841
(foreign language)

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.300
Dr. NakaMats saw the
cancer as an opportunity.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.630
It was his greatest challenge

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:11.000
to invent his way out
of an impossible corner.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.850
He developed his own
personal cancer treatment.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.830
This includes a
meticulously documented diet

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.690
and a new invention to fight the cancer

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.933
he calls the Gangan Robot.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.760
The doctors gave him one year to live.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.897
That was five years ago.

00:04:32.463 --> 00:04:35.655
(spirited orchestral music)

00:04:35.655 --> 00:04:38.572
(foreign language)

